    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "graph",
      "title": "Calculation cache",
      "datasource": "prometheus",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "span": 6,
      "fill": 1,
      "stack": true,
      "linewidth": 2,
      "nullPointMode": "null",
      "legend": {
        "show": true,
        "current": true,
        "max": true,
        "values": true
      },
      "tooltip": {
        "shared": true,
        "sort": 2,
        "value_type": "individual"
      },
      "yaxes": [
        {
          "format": "reqps",
          "show": true,
          "min": 0
        },
        {
          "format": "short",
          "show": false
        }
      ],
      "xaxis": {
        "mode": "time",
        "show": true
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (rate(chemclaw_calc_cache_total[15m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(chemclaw_calc_cache_seconds_saved_total[15m]))",
          "legendFormat": "calculator seconds saved/s",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Lookups by outcome, and what they were worth. `hit` answered from the store, `shared` joined another caller's in-flight computation, `miss` computed. The seconds series is the wall clock those hits and shares did not spend \u2014 a thousand avoided millisecond lookups and one avoided nineteen-minute CREST search are the same number of lookups and not the same saving, so read the rate against the count rather than instead of it."
    },
