    {
      "id": 21,
      "type": "graph",
      "title": "Refusals the ledger's growth bound deleted",
      "description": "`ingest_rejections` keeps the newest 1,000 refusals per source, on the argument that a source refusing more than that has one systematic defect its newest thousand rows describe as well as a million would. That is an assumption about the *distribution* of a source's refusals, not a fact about any source: one with more distinct one-off refusals than the cap loses its oldest permanently, and `refusals_matching` then reports those records as never refused \u2014 the record gone rather than unread. A flat zero is the assumption holding. A source with a steady rate here is one whose refusal history is being destroyed faster than anyone reads it.",
      "gridPos": {
